TASK DESCRIPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Objective: Transition the CIRO multi-agent orchestration engine from a single-crisis
             (flood) response system to a multi-crisis (flood and heatwave) platform.
             Validate the end-to-end intelligence pipeline, resolve any environment
             crashes, and ensure 100% stability for the live hackathon demonstration.

  Scope    :
    1. Update the database schema to support disaster types.
    2. Expand mock telemetry tools (weather) to simulate heatwave indicators.
    3. Revamp system prompts for all 8 specialized agents to handle dual-crisis branching.
    4. Fix test environment instabilities (asyncio event loop closures, UTF-8 encoding).
    5. Run and validate the full end-to-end pipeline test suite against a live DB.

